From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:55:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Cheats off by default; the host's choice governs both
 players

Previously the launchers force-enabled the $XD OU Fixes AR code on every
launch and on every netplay start. That made cheats mandatory and, worse,
a host/guest mismatch (one side forced on, the other in a different state)
was a turn-1 desync risk.

Now cheats are OFF by default on both platforms. A launcher control -- a
checkbox on desktop, a switch on Android -- lets a player enable the
$XD OU Fixes code. In netplay only the HOST'S choice matters: NETPLAY_SYNC_CODES
stays on, so if the host enables the code it is synced to the guest and both
run it; if the host leaves it off, both play clean. The code is never force
-enabled anywhere, so the two sides can no longer disagree.

This makes Orre Colosseum (cheat-off, its own in-save ruleset) the default
experience while keeping the OU bring-6-pick-4 format one toggle away. PBR
mode's own cheat handling is unchanged.
